Subject: [PATCH] Defer XML-RPC shutdown until its queued callback returns

fldigi.terminate runs through qrunner. Closing the main window deletes
that queue in exit_process while fqueue::pop still needs to destroy the
current callback and advance its ring buffer, causing a use-after-free.
Schedule the close through FLTK so the qrunner callback can finish first.

--- a/src/network/xmlrpc.cxx
+++ b/src/network/xmlrpc.cxx
@@ -510 +510,2 @@
-		fl_digi_main->do_callback();
+		// Shutdown deletes the queue executing this callback. Defer it.
+		Fl::add_timeout(0.0, [](void*) { fl_digi_main->do_callback(); });
